# Model collaboration policy

**Constitution:** [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md) — *CONSTITUTION FOR AGENTS AND SUBAGENTS* (canonical roles, §2 workflow, guardrails).

This rule **enforces** the constitution in Cursor. Setup detail: [MODEL_COLLABORATION.md](../../docs/agent/MODEL_COLLABORATION.md).

| Model | NVIDIA id | Role |
|-------|-----------|------|
| **GLM-5.1** | `z-ai/glm-5.1` | **Lead** — plan, handoff, review, approve |
| **Qwen3-Coder** | `qwen/qwen3-coder-480b-a35b-instruct` | **Implementer subagent** — scoped diffs only |
| **Auto / other** | Cursor router | Same guardrails; no freelancing scope |

Qwen is **GLM's subagent**, not a parallel architect.

## When GLM-5.1 is active

- Inspect wiki ([handoff](../../docs/research_wiki/handoff.md)) before directing work.
- Produce **implementation handoff** ([template](../../docs/research_wiki/templates/model-handoff.md)).
- **Delegate** to `qwen-implementer` — do not land large mechanical patches unless user asks.
- Review Qwen output against handoff before acceptance.

Slash: `/glm-plan` · Subagent: [`glm-lead`](../../.cursor/agents/glm-lead.md)

## When Qwen3-Coder is active

- Implement **only** approved GLM handoff (or user paste with Goal / In scope / Out of scope / Files / Steps / Tests).
- Missing or ambiguous handoff → **stop and ask**; do not replan or expand scope.
- Return: changed files, rationale, tests run.

Slash: `/qwen-implement` · Subagent: [`qwen-implementer`](../../.cursor/agents/qwen-implementer.md)

## When Auto or another model is active

- Follow [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md) §3 duties and §6 guardrails.
- Non-trivial code: prefer GLM handoff + Qwen implement pattern; do not bypass facit rules.

## Guardrails (all models)

Human fib = facit · `*_candidate` ≠ facit · wiki = navigation · source code/docs = truth.

Inspect / Observed vs Assumptions: [repo-aware-coding-agent.mdc](repo-aware-coding-agent.mdc).
